    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d557">

                <pb facs="0778" n="764" sameAs="frus:frus1944v06/pg764"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/15324: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-03-31T16:00:00+07:00">March 31, 1944—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 9:22 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>569. Rice<anchor n="14" xml:id="d557-f1"/> reports from Lanchow under date March
                    26 that it is rumored there that a Moslem force under Ma Chung-ying (Kansu
                    Moslem leader driven out of Sinkiang by Sheng Shih-tsai in 1933–34 and rumored
                    since to have been residing in United States [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >U.S.S.R</hi>]) has occupied areas north and west of Tihwa, including
                    Ining.</p>
                <pb facs="0779" n="765" xml:id="pg765"/>
                <p>A rumor current here is to effect that Ma with Russian support including 4 planes
                    is leading rebellion in Kashgar region of south Sinkiang. It is possible these
                    rumors may have been inspired by alleged bombing attacks reported in Embassy’s
                    561, March 30 and previous, and may represent Chinese attempt to impugn Russia’s
                    attitude toward Sinkiang similar to efforts along this line mentioned in last
                    paragraph of Embassy’s despatch 1937, December 21.<anchor n="15"
                        xml:id="d557-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>Tihwa is being instructed to report by telegraph.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
